  "question": {
    "prompt": "\\(2:3=8:x\\). What is \\(x\\)? Calculate: \\(8\\times3\\div2=?\\)"
  },
  "schemaVersion": "3.0",
  "solutions": [
    {
      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_p210",
        "cnm_p145"
      ],
      "explanation": "\\(2x=24\\), \\(x=12\\).",
      "id": "cross-products",
      "sourceRef": "cn-math/cnm_p211_q1#cross-products",
      "title": "Use cross-products"
    },
    {
      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_p107"
      ],
      "explanation": "Multiplying both terms of a ratio by the same nonzero number leaves its quotient unchanged. Since \\(8=2\\times4\\), multiply both terms of \\(2:3\\) by \\(4\\):\n\\[\n2:3=(2\\times4):(3\\times4)=8:12.\n\\]\nTherefore \\(x=12\\), which is nonzero as required for \\(8:x\\).",
      "id": "equivalent-ratio-scaling",
      "sourceRef": "cn-math/cnm_p211_q1#equivalent-ratio-scaling",
      "title": "Scale both ratio terms"
    }
